# LF everywhere, checked out as LF on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. `bin/pres` is a `sh` script, and a CRLF checkout makes
# its shebang unrunnable on Linux and macOS with an error that names neither the
# file nor the line endings. The deck sources are the second reason: markdown is
# the source of truth here because it diffs, and a checkout that rewrites every
# line ending produces a diff of the whole file the first time anyone touches it
# on the other kind of machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Renders and figures that are not text. Nothing here is committed today —
# output/ is gitignored — but a professor who moves one into the repository
# should not have it corrupted on the way in.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.mp4 binary
